The `<?hide>` tag is a legacy HTML/CSS element that browsers ignore, so it won't affect your layout. For modern CSS, `display: none` is the standard way to hide an element while keeping its structure.

If you are building a table, the `<th>` tags are semantic and should remain visible in your HTML even if you hide them visually. You can use CSS to hide them from sighted users but keep them in the DOM for screen readers and search engines.

Here is how you would structure that in CSS:

```css
